From: Alex Perrin <44126061+AlexPerrin@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 00:54:20 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] feat: Vampyre Slayer quest and the Blue Moon Inn bartender
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Problem. Vampyre Slayer was not implemented. Morgan always gave his
after-quest lines (the draynor script asked "completed?", which the
default assume-completed quest mode always answers with yes), and the
Blue Moon Inn had no bartender, so the quest's beer step could not be
done.

Change. New quest on the OSRS progress varp 178 (`varp.vampire`) through
the server-only varbit `vampyre_slayer_progress`: 0, 1 started, 2 stake
received, 3 complete (the cache dbrow end state, checked at startup).
These are the values Quest Helper keys its steps on. Morgan and Dr
Harlow follow the OSRS Wiki transcripts (start, legends, garlic hint,
Harlow's beer, stake, topics, a lost stake); Harlow's client varbits
`harlow_given_beer`/`harlow_given_stake` are set. Morgan's garlic
cupboard opens and gives garlic. Opening the coffin in the manor
basement at stages 1-2 raises Count Draynor for that player (500-tick
lifespan, removed on logout). Garlic in the inventory weakens him
(-10 hitpoints, -10 Attack/Strength, -40 Defence). At 0 hitpoints a
stake and a hammer finish him (quest complete: 3 QP, 4,825 Attack XP);
otherwise he regenerates to full. Morgan's after-quest dialogue moves
from DraynorVillageNpcs into the quest. New `BlueMoonBartender`
(transcript): "A glass of your finest ale please." sells a beer for 2
coins, plus the fortune and equipment topics.

Tests. `VampyreSlayerInteractionTest` (5): start, decline, Harlow's
beer before the stake, a lost stake replaced, Morgan's garlic hint. `:content:quest:test`. Manual: a
full run with Quest Helper 4.18 on the RuneLite desktop client (fresh
account): every step showed the right QH text, varp 178 went 0-1-2-3,
the bartender's beer turned QH's requirement green, and the kill
completed the quest.

Data sources. Dialogue: OSRS Wiki transcripts (Morgan, Dr Harlow,
Bartender (Blue Moon Inn), Vampyre Slayer). Rewards, garlic effects and
locations: OSRS Wiki quest page. Step values: Quest Helper's
VampyreSlayer and the cache dbrow `quest_vampyreslayer`.

Caveats. Guesses: the cupboard's take message, "The coffin is sealed
shut." outside the quest, the Count's attack animation, and keeping the
stake after the kill. Simplified: the garlic weakening lasts until he
respawns (the wiki ties it to the first melee hit and 30 seconds); his
fast regeneration and return to the coffin are not implemented. Needs
the quest-module patch 12 (QuestTalkFixture).

